ial set for each positive closed time slab, with the same fixed q. dt, dx and lap are the usual time partial, standard-coordinate spatial partial, and componentwise sum of second partials on that smooth domain. e has the exact sum of Euclidean squared norms and no factor 1/2; energy is its Lebesgue integral. The conclusion asserts absolute integrability at every positive time, differentiability on the positive half-line, zero ordinary derivative at every positive time, and equality at every pair of positive times. Conversely these are exactly the specified conclusions for the restriction; any choice of extension has identical positive-time densities and energy. No hypothesis or conclusion about nonpositive times is added.\"}}},\"library_terms\":{}}}","status":"completed"}}

