 Set.Icc s t, u (x,r) = q), (∀ t : ℝ, 0 < t → Integrable (fun x => WM.e u (x,t))) ∧ DifferentiableOn ℝ (WM.energy u) (Set.Ioi 0) ∧ (∀ t : ℝ, 0 < t → deriv (WM.energy u) t = 0) ∧ (∀ s t : ℝ, 0 < s → 0 < t → WM.energy u s = WM.energy u t)\",\"correspondence\":{\"mode\":\"equivalent\",\"explanation\":\"n,m are natural dimensions with H001 imposing n,m≥1, the same admissible integer dimensions. X n is ℝ^n in its standard coordinates with product Lebesgue measure; its auxiliary sup norm gives the same finite-dimensional smooth structure as Euclidean coordinates. Y m has exactly the Euclidean norm and dot product. A positive-time u extends to our total parameter by q for t≤0; any total parameter restricts to the original map. H002 is smoothness only on the open positive-time domain, so these operations preserve it in both directions; all partial derivatives and their iterates at positive times depend only on that germ. H003 and H004 are exactly unit-vector and sphere constraints. H005 quantifies a separate real scalar at each point, with no regularity or selection assumption. H006 is precisely one compact spatial set for each positive closed time slab, with the same fixed q. dt, dx and lap are the usual time partial, standard-coordinate spatial partial, and componentwise sum of second partials on that smooth domain. e has the exact sum of Euclidean squared norms and no factor 1/2; energy is its Lebesgue integral. The conclusion asserts absolute integrability at every positive time, differentiability on the positive half-line, zero ordinary derivative at every positive time, and equality at every pair of positive times. Conversely these are exactly the specified conclusions for the restriction; any choice of extension has identical positive-time densities and energy. No hypothesis or conclusion about nonpositive times is added.\"}}},\"library_terms\":{}}}","status":"completed"}],"error":null,"incomplete_details":null,"tools":[{"type":"function","name":"search_mathlib","description":"在固定 mathlib 的 Lean 源码中搜索正则表达式，返回至多 100 行。","parameters":{"type":"object","properties":{"query":{"type":"string"}},"required":["query"],"additionalProperties":false},"output_schema":null,"strict":false},{"type":"function","name":"read_mathlib","description":"读取固定 mathlib 中一个 Mathlib/...lean 文件的指定行。","parameters":{"type":"object","properties":{"path":{"type":"string"},"start_line":{"type":"integer"},"line_count":{"type":"integer"}},"required":["path","start_line","line_count"],"additionalProperties":false},"output_schema":null,"strict":false},{"type":"function","name":"read_task_input","description":"Read one declared frozen document. For JSON use pointer (empty string lists the root); large objects return keys, and strings resume with offset=next_offset. For text use inclusive start/end lines and column=next_column when continuing a long line. Every serialized result is at most 32 KiB. Follow has_more and the returned continuation coordinates; no arbitrary local files are accessible.","parameters":{"type":"object","properties":{"id":{"type":"string"},"start":{"type":"integer"},"end":{"type":"integer"},"column":{"type":"integer"},"pointer":{"type":"string"},"offset":{"type":"integer"},"limit":{"type":"integer"}},"required":["id"],"additionalProperties":false},"output_schema":null,"strict":false},{"type":"function","name":"read_yui","description":"Read declared Yui rules/templates; no tests, historical runs or personal files.","parameters":{"type":"object","properties":{"path":{"type":"string"},"start":{"type":"integer"},"end":{"type":"integer"},"column":{"type":"integer"}},"required":["path","start","end"],"additionalProperties":false},"output_schema":null,"strict":false},{"type":"function","name":"check_artifact","description":"Check a JSON artifact against the explicit stage contract; this is not automatic mathematical certification.","parameters":{"type":"object","properties":{"artifact_json":{"type":"string"}},"required":["artifact_json"],"additionalPro